"full_name": "Itano, W.M."}, {"full_name": "Wineland, D.J."}]}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1190245"}}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "Springer"}, "label": "6", "misc": ["Handbook of Stochastic Processes for Physics, Chemistry and the Natural Sciences, ( Verlag, Berlin, 1985)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Gardiner, C.W."}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "7", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "40", "artid": "1195", "year": 1993, "page_start": "1195", "journal_title": "J.Mod.Opt."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Shore, B.W."}, {"full_name": "Knight, P.L."}]}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2904348"}}, {"reference": {"label": "8", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "8", "artid": "541", "year": 1996, "page_start": "541", "journal_title": "Quant.Semiclass.Opt."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Dyrting, S."}, {"full_name": "Milburn, G.J."}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "9", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "44", "artid": "5401", "year": 1991, "page_start": "5401", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Milburn, G.J."}]}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2733673"}}, {"reference": {"label": "10", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "48", "artid": "3900", "year": 1993, "page_start": "3900", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Moya-Cessa, H."}, {"full_name": "Buzek, V."}, {"full_name": "Kim, M.S."}, {"full_name": "Knight, P.L."}]}}, {"reference": {"label": "11", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "56", "artid": "3139", "year": 1997, "page_start": "3139", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Kuang, L.-M."}, {"full_name": "Chen, X."}, {"full_name": "Chen, G.-H."}, {"full_name": "Ge, M.-L."}]}}], "number_of_pages": 14, "referenced_authors_bais": ["D.J.Wineland.1", "D.M.Meekhof.2", "D.M.Meekhof.1", "B.E.King.1", "W.M.Itano.4", "G.J.Milburn.1", "C.Monroe.2", "B.W.Shore.1", "Peter.Knight.1"], "figures": [{"filename": "fig1.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Internal level scheme of $^9$Be$^+$. The ground state $|g\\rangle$ is the $2s\\ ^2S_{1/2}$ ($F=2, M_F = 2$) state and the excited state $|e \\rangle$ is the $2s\\ ^2S_{1/2}$ ($F=1, M_F = 1$) state. The state $|g\\rangle$ is detected by applying a nearly resonant $\\sigma^+$ polarized laser probe field to drive a strong transition between $|g\\rangle$ and another state $^2P_{3/2}$ ($F=3, M_F = 3$) as indicated. As this other state can only decay back to $|g\\rangle$, any fluorescence observed on this transition is evidence that the atom was in the state $|g\\rangle$ at the start of the probe pulse.", "label": "fig1", "source": "arxiv", "key": "5ea4b7475d9d5e22f51c014b91ef4c7e", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/5ea4b7475d9d5e22f51c014b91ef4c7e"}, {"filename": "fig2.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "$P_g(t)$ for an initial $|g, n=0\\rangle$ state of the atom driven by the first blue sideband, Eq.~(32). The time parameter $\\tau = \\Omega_0 t$ is scaled with the effective Rabi frequency $\\Omega_0 = 470$ kHz. The value for the scaled damping coefficient $\\Gamma^\\prime = \\Gamma \\Omega_0$ is 0.041 and the one for $\\eta$ is 0.2. All the values are rough estimates from the experimental values given in [3].", "label": "fig2", "source": "arxiv", "key": "ac3ecf2685ae9767d7b209fee7a13812", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/ac3ecf2685ae9767d7b209fee7a13812"}], "legacy_version": "20150616122635.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "1997-10-21", "preprint_date": "1997-10", "author_count": 2, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "2 figures, submitted to PRA"}], "first_author": {"full_name": "Schneider, S.", "last_name": "Schneider", "first_name": "S.", "recid": 1027154}, "control_number": 449990, "dois": [{"source": "ADS", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.57.3748"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.57.3748"}], "earliest_date": "1997-10", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Schneider:1997mu"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We consider one source of decoherence for a single trapped ion due to intensity and phase fluctuations in the exciting laser pulses. For simplicity we assume that the stochastic processes involved are white noise processes, which enables us to give a simple master equation description of this source of decoherence. This master equation is averaged over the noise, and is sufficient to describe the results of experiments that probe the oscillations in the electronic populations as energy is exchanged between the internal and electronic motion. Our results are in good qualitative agreement with recent experiments and predict that the decoherence rate will depend on vibrational quantum number in different ways depending on which vibrational excitation sideband is used."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "We consider one source of decoherence for a single trapped ion due to intensity and phase fluctuations in the exciting laser pulses. For simplicity we assume that the stochastic processes involved are white noise processes, which enables us to give a simple master equation description of this source of decoherence. This master equation is averaged over the noise, and is sufficient to describe the results of experiments that probe the oscillations in the electronic populations as energy is exchanged between the internal and electronic motion. Our results are in good qualitative agreement with recent experiments and predict that the decoherence rate will depend on vibrational quantum number in different ways depending on which vibrational excitation sideband is used.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "1998PhRvA..57.3748S"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-3643158"}], "titles": [{"title": "Decoherence in ion traps due to laser intensity and phase fluctuations"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "Decoherence in ion traps due to laser intensity and phase fluctuations"}], "facet_author_name": ["1027154_Stephen E. Schneider", "1062536_Gerard J. Milburn"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:449990", "updated": "2025-10-01T10:40:15.806646"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys. Rev. A", "Phys.Rev.A"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/9710044"}]}, "created": "1997-10-21T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "449990"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.57.3748&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}